<div class="prose about-page">
  <p class="section-label">About</p>
  <h1>I'm Phil Venice.</h1>
  <p>This is my personal site. I write about books and articles I'm reading, things I'm building,
    and questions I'm trying to work through. Some posts draw on my professional experience.
    Others start with something that caught my attention.</p>
  <p>My background is in supply chain risk, third-party risk, and enterprise program leadership.
    I spent 11 years at Boeing and now work in product management at LMI.</p>
  <p>I'm interested in how systems work, how people make decisions, and what happens when an idea
    meets the constraints of putting it into practice. Writing helps me examine what I think
    and where I still have questions.</p>
  <p>You'll find finished essays here alongside shorter notes, projects, and things I'm learning about.</p>
  <p>These are my own views.</p>
  <p><a href="/blog/">Read my writing</a> or <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.</p>
</div>
